---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /archive/
title: Archive
---
{#- One page, by month (2026-11-26; 20 a page with the pager before). Each
    way through the writing has one job: skimming backward is the home
    stream's pager, a topic is the shelf and subject pages, and the archive
    is time and titles. One page so Ctrl-F finds a title; a year of dailies
    is ~365 short rows, so split by year only when that stops being true.
    Reached from the footer on every page. -#}
<h1>Archive</h1>
{% set oldest = collections.stream | last %}
<p class="archive-count">{{ collections.stream | length }} posts since {{ (oldest.essay or oldest.post).date | readableDate }}</p>
{% for entry in collections.stream %}
{% set item = entry.essay or entry.post %}
{% set ds = item.date | dateSlug %}
{% set m = ds.slice(0, 7) %}
{% set prev = collections.stream[loop.index0 - 1] if not loop.first %}
{% if loop.first or ((prev.essay or prev.post).date | dateSlug).slice(0, 7) != m %}
{% if not loop.first %}</ul></section>{% endif %}
{% set rd = item.date | readableDate %}
<section class="archive-month">
<h2 class="archive-month-head">{{ rd.split(" ").slice(1).join(" ") }}</h2>
<ul class="archive-list">
{% endif %}
  <li>
    <span class="archive-day">{{ ds.slice(8) | int }}</span>
    {% if entry.kind == "essay" %}
    <span class="archive-entry"><span class="archive-kind">deep thoughts</span> <a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.title }}</a></span>
    {% else %}
    <a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title or (item.date | readableDate) }}</a>
    {% endif %}
  </li>
{% if loop.last %}</ul></section>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
